Comment: Sparky Stereo OS, Daniel Ramos's (Capitain Jack) edition of SparkyLinux (https://sparkylinux.org, by
 Paweł "pavroo" Pijanowski). The engine follows what Linux, Debian and KDE already have: the systemd journal's
 message catalogs and MESSAGE_ID (Lennart Poettering and the systemd contributors), systemd's OnFailure= with
 top-level drop-ins and $MONITOR_* (systemd.unit(5), systemd.exec(5)), polkit's pkexec (David Zeuthen and the
 polkit contributors), and KDE's plasma-disks (Harald Sitter) for how a system problem reaches a person, with a
 reversible Ignore. No code is copied from them. Built with cgm-zig, Daniel Ramos's fork of Zig (the Zig Software
 Foundation and contributors).

